 #### url
 
-The URL to test. `https://www.gstatic.com/generate_204` will be used if empty.
+The URL to test. `https://cp.cloudflare.com/generate_204` will be used if empty.
+
+When the URL hostname resolves to both IPv4 and IPv6, the test also records
+each address family's TCP and UDP availability for the actual outbound.
+TCP uses HTTP; UDP uses HTTP/3 and requires `with_quic`. The displayed delay
+is the minimum successful measurement. A single-stack URL leaves both
+families unknown and retains the ordinary TCP delay test.
+
+TCP and UDP use the same rule: a successful probe is available and a failed
+probe is unavailable. The configured URL must support the tested protocols.
+Unknown means a probe was not performed or the build cannot perform it, not
+that an HTTP/3 failure lacks confirmation from another probe. UDP requires an
+HTTPS URL and does not fall back to TCP.
+The probes run concurrently within the normal test timeout. An API request's
+shorter deadline still applies. Same-host alternative UDP ports advertised by
+`Alt-Svc` are used without changing the HTTP origin or TLS server name.
+
+For RealIP connections, the destination family is adapted only
+when the selected outbound has a known available alternative. Address
+association uses observed DNS answers, never sniffed SNI. The association index
+stores query context, not another DNS response cache, and does not require the
+original address to remain cached.
+The other family is queried through the original DNS transport with the resolved
+query options. The original DNS client uses its normal cache, optimistic refresh
+and expiration policy; a cache miss or disabled caching causes a live query.
+Adaptation does not repeat DNS rule evaluation or server selection;
+supplemental answers update the same DNS association cache. Direct and
+FakeIP connections retain their existing behavior. Missing query associations
+leave the original destination unchanged. The public `reverse_mapping`
+option retains its original behavior independently of adaptation.
+
+The Android and yacd integrations show one dot per address family: green when
+both TCP and UDP are available, red when neither is available, and yellow when
+only one is available. A family with an unknown result has no dot.
+Without `with_quic`, UDP is not probed and the dots reflect TCP availability alone.
+The UDP capability itself remains unknown.
+
+Connection details and outbound logs use the adapted destination.
 
 #### interval
 
